\par \pard\plain \s46\loch\qj\qj\ltrpar{\loch
The east quay was built in three stages. The first stage, a timber jetty of twenty berths, dates from the start of the register; the second doubled it in stone, and the third, the long breakwater, shelters both from the south-west swell. Every berth has a number, a length in metres and a holder. The register is kept on paper and in a table; the two are compared each spring, and the differences are explained in the notes of the harbour master.}
