The east quay was built in three stages. The first stage, a timber jetty of twenty berths, dates from the start of the register; the second doubled it in stone, and the third, the long breakwater, shelters both from the south-west swell. Every berth has a number, a length in metres and a holder. The register is kept on paper and in a table; the two are compared each spring, and the differences are explained in the notes of the harbour master. Visitors are asked to call the harbour office on channel 9 before they come in, to give the length of their boat and its draught, and to say how many nights they plan to stay. The east quay was built in three stages. The first stage, a timber jetty of twenty berths, dates from the start of the register; the second doubled it in stone, and the third, the long breakwater, shelters both from the south-west swell. }
